# Git Workflow
- Before non-trivial edits inspect git status, current branch and baseline commit.
- Preserve existing user changes; never discard them to simplify work.
- No force push, destructive reset/clean, history rewrite, rebase, amend or squash on published history unless explicitly requested and safe.
- Stage/commit only task-related files with coherent descriptive commits.
- Never commit secrets, local env files, machine caches, build artifacts or unrelated generated output.
- Review final diff for accidental deletion, formatting churn, dependency drift, debug code and weakened tests.
- Use the baseline commit as rollback anchor.
- Never silently switch repo/branch/backup/archive; a user-declared official root/version/hash remains authoritative until changed.
